      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The beta-receptor blocker Timolol was investigated for 28 weeks in a double blind trial and then for up to 100 weeks in an open trial in patients with angina pectoris. In both phases of the investigation. Timolol caused a quite marked regression in the frequency of attacks and in the pulse rate at rest. The evaluation of therapeutic success by doctor and patient was positive for Timolol."},
